# --- LitCodex publication boundary ---
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: npm resolves ignores as `files[]` -> .npmignore -> .gitignore.
# This package has no `files[]` allowlist, so before this file existed npm fell back to
# .gitignore. The moment .npmignore appears that fallback is DISABLED ENTIRELY, so every
# rule below must mirror .gitignore or previously-excluded local state starts publishing.
#
# KEEP IN SYNC WITH .gitignore. When you add a rule there, add it here. Verify with the
# JSON output — the human-readable listing wraps long paths and cannot be diffed reliably:
#   npm pack --dry-run --json | node -e "let s='';process.stdin.on('data',d=>s+=d).on('end',()=>console.log(JSON.parse(s)[0].files.length))"
# Baseline: 1216 files. Removing this file entirely yields 1217 — the difference is exactly
# AGENTS.md, which is how the switch to .npmignore was proven behavior-preserving.

# Dependencies & build output
node_modules/
/dist/
packages/*/dist/
plugins/litcodex/dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# EXCEPTION — Codex MARKETPLACE distribution channel. `codex plugin add` copies the plugin
# tree verbatim (no build, no `npm install`), so the compiled component `dist/` and the rules
# component's vendored picomatch MUST ship or every hook crashes with MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
!plugins/litcodex/components/*/dist/
!plugins/litcodex/components/rules/node_modules/
!plugins/litcodex/components/rules/node_modules/picomatch/
!plugins/litcodex/components/rules/node_modules/picomatch/**

# Local planning state (NEVER published)
HANDOFF.md
plans/

# Canonical byte-identical lit-handoff source assets are product payload, not local state.
!plugins/litcodex/vendor/handoff/templates/HANDOFF.md
!plugins/litcodex/vendor/handoff/examples/HANDOFF-example-generic-auth-refactor.md

# LitCodex runtime + evidence state (NEVER published)
.litcodex/
plugins/litcodex/skills/lit-humanizer/fixtures/negative/

# Sibling-harness dogfooding state written into this worktree by other lit tools.
# Was leaking into the published tarball until 2026-08-01 (3 session files).
.litclaude/

# Temp QA scratch
.tmp/
tmp/
*.tmp
.qa-tmp/
litcodex-qa-*/

# Packed tarballs
*.tgz
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# Environment & OS noise
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Read-only reference archive (lives only in the parent workspace; never copy in)
\# REFERENCE/

# Local agent navigation guidance: tracked in git so contributors and in-repo agents see it,
# never shipped to the registry.
AGENTS.md

# Documentation artwork and release operations stay in Git, outside npm payloads.
# These publication-only exclusions intentionally do not belong in .gitignore.
/cover.png
/generate_cover.py
/docs/assets/
/docs/release/
/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md
